      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "An elderly man who had incapacitating angina, despite coronary artery surgery and maximal medical management was deliberately made hypothyroid with radio-iodine. Five years later he was virtually free of chest pain. There is still a limited number of patients in whom this is a useful form of therapy, despite the attendant morbidity of myxoedema."},
